      "value": "@{69e7497065c4cf9dd920e335|full_name} Thank you very much for providing a repro avatar.\n\nThe contact receiver toggled by this expressions option appears to be behaving as intended. It is not detecting the avatar's own head, or any of the other body parts it's configured to match. You can see this for yourself if you open the action menu and go to Options->Avatar->Debug and then find the parameter controlled by this contact receiver - from what I'm seeing, it never moves off zero until it hits a matching contact sender on someone else's avatar.\n\nThere appears to be a sphere with a custom shader around the avatar's head whose scale is controlled by an animator. I can see that the scale of this sphere is 0.3 when the above parameter is 0, and 0.125 when it's 1. At the lowest scale, it clips into your head, so it's only visible when your head is not near someone else's. This seems to be the wrong way round based on what you've described - can you please check if that's the case? Would swapping them give you the effect you're looking for?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
